# WhatsApp Messaging Tier Visibility

Add per-account messaging tier, quality rating, and live usage to the CRM dashboard so operators know their limits before running a broadcast.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Caching strategy decision** — see Open Questions Q1. The answer determines whether we add fields to `whatsapp_config` or create a new `whatsapp_limits` table.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **BullMQ scheduler vs NestJS `@Cron`** — you already have BullMQ wired. The plan proposes a BullMQ repeatable job for the sync, consistent with your existing infrastructure. If you prefer `@nestjs/schedule` (`@Cron`), that's a simpler drop-in but won't show up in your BullMQ dashboard.

> [!WARNING]
> **New Prisma migration** — one new SQL migration is required to add the limit/rating columns (or new table). No destructive changes to existing rows.

> [!CAUTION]
> **Access token refresh** — the `embedded_signup` token (`token_expires_at` already tracked) must be refreshed before calling the Meta Graph API in the sync job. If expired, the job skips the account and emits a warning log; the UI shows a "token expired — reconnect" state. This is not implemented today and **is a prerequisite for embedded_signup accounts**.

