## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1 — Schema placement**: Should the tier/rating data live as new columns on `whatsapp_config`, or in a separate `whatsapp_limits` table?  
> - **Inline (recommended)** — `whatsapp_config` already has one row per account; adding ~4 nullable columns keeps it simple and avoids a JOIN everywhere.  
> - **Separate table** — better if you plan to store a historical audit trail (e.g. "tier changed from 1K→10K on date X") or want to track portfolio-level numbers. Adds a JOIN.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2 — Sync interval**: How often should we poll Meta for tier + quality rating?  
> - **Every 6 hours (recommended)** — tier changes are rare; quality rating moves slowly. Keeps API calls well under any rate limits.  
> - **Every 1 hour** — more responsive but 6× the API calls across all accounts.  
> - **On-demand only** — only fetch when the user opens the dashboard widget (cache TTL = 6 h). Simpler but loses push updates.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q3 — Live usage source**: The "messages sent in the rolling 24-hour window" counter is **not available directly from the Meta Graph API**. Two options:  
> - **Count from your own DB** (recommended) — `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM broadcast_recipients WHERE account_id=? AND status IN ('sent','delivered','read') AND sent_at > NOW()-INTERVAL '24h'`. No extra API call. Limitation: only counts broadcast messages, not automation/flow/inbox sends.  
> - **Aggregate across all send sources** — requires tagging every outbound message (broadcasts + automations + flows + inbox) with `sent_at` in a central ledger. More accurate but a larger cross-cutting change.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q4 — Portfolio-level numbers**: If a WABA has multiple phone numbers under it, Meta enforces a single shared limit across all of them. Do you want to show the portfolio limit (WABA-level) alongside the per-number usage, or show only per-number metrics?

> [!NOTE]
> **Q5 — Broadcast pre-flight gate**: Should the broadcast composer hard-block submission if `remaining < recipients`? Or only show a warning banner and let the user proceed?

