## Proposed Changes

### 1 — Data Model

---

#### [NEW] Migration `049_whatsapp_messaging_limits.sql`

Adds four nullable columns to `whatsapp_config` (inline approach, see Q1):

```sql
ALTER TABLE whatsapp_config
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS messaging_limit_tier  TEXT
    CHECK (messaging_limit_tier IN ('TIER_250', 'TIER_1K', 'TIER_10K', 'TIER_100K', 'UNLIMITED')),
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS quality_rating        TEXT
    CHECK (quality_rating IN ('GREEN', 'YELLOW', 'RED', 'UNKNOWN')),
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS tier_daily_limit      INTEGER,      -- denormalized int: 250, 1000, 10000, 100000, NULL=unlimited
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS limits_synced_at      TIMESTAMPTZ;  -- NULL = never synced

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_whatsapp_config_limits_synced_at
  ON whatsapp_config (limits_synced_at)
  WHERE limits_synced_at IS NOT NULL;
```

**Tier → limit mapping** (maintained in code, not DB):

| `messaging_limit_tier` | `tier_daily_limit` | Label shown in UI |
|---|---|---|
| `TIER_250` | 250 | Unverified (250/day) |
| `TIER_1K` | 1,000 | Tier 1 (1K/day) |
| `TIER_10K` | 10,000 | Tier 2 (10K/day) |
| `TIER_100K` | 100,000 | Tier 3 (100K/day) |
| `UNLIMITED` | NULL | Unlimited |
| `NULL` | NULL | Not synced yet |

**Caching strategy**: Polling sync every **6 hours** (BullMQ repeatable job). The data is stale-tolerable; tier changes happen at most daily. The UI always shows `limits_synced_at` so the user knows the age of the data. A manual "Refresh" button on the widget triggers a live re-fetch.

