### 5 — Edge Cases

| Scenario | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| Account never synced (`limits_synced_at IS NULL`) | UI shows a "Checking limits…" shimmer on first mount; if GET returns `tier: null`, shows "Limits not yet loaded — click Refresh." |
| `TIER_250` (unverified) | Dedicated blue info banner: "Upgrade your tier in Meta Business Manager." Link to Meta docs. No red warning — it's expected state. |
| Token expired (`tokenExpired: true`) | Sync job skips account. UI shows amber banner with reconnect CTA. Does NOT block broadcasts (credentials still work for sending). |
| Portfolio-level shared limit (Q4) | If `waba_id` is set, the `fetchWabaPhoneNumbers` call returns all numbers under the WABA. If there are >1 numbers, show a note: "Limit shared across N phone numbers under this WABA." |
| Meta API down (sync job) | Job catches HTTP errors, does NOT update `limits_synced_at`. On next run it retries. UI continues showing last known data + stale indicator if `limits_synced_at > 12h ago`. |
| `quality_rating = RED` | Non-blocking amber warning on broadcast composer: "Your number's quality rating is Red. Meta may pause message delivery. Avoid sending bulk messages until it recovers." |

